Negative control for the count's departure from the refinements row (H1 · G5 ·
AC4.4).

Puts the count back. The row regains a meta count after its actions — the exact
pre-H1 arrangement (`G5` ordered the actions ahead of the count; `H1` then took
the count out of this row altogether and gave it to the display row's Results
label). Nothing else moves: the chips, Clear all, the removal write and the
clear write are untouched, so what goes red is the one claim under test — this
row carries NO count.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: refinements-row.spec.ts — the no-count case, however it is measured: the
row renders no `data-test-key="refinements-count"` element, no `labs.results_*`
count label, and no tally of its own chips.

